autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "2b0b90d9-dd4f-41c1-ab51-1ec86d039743", "created_at": "2026-09-17T10:41:06.913199", "failure_effects": ["V bekr\u00e4ftar sitt st\u00f6d och sin tolerans f\u00f6r den S-ledda minoritetsregeringen, villkorat av en stark, synlig och bindande inflytandemekanism.", "V:s krav p\u00e5 en stark, synlig och bindande inflytandemekanism (formellt samarbetsavtal, budgetmekanism, att inte kringg\u00e5s) tillgodoses inte fullt ut; V:s st\u00f6d f\u00f6rblir villkorat och V signalerar att man utan reellt inflytande kan \u00f6verg\u00e5 till opposition, vilket \u00f6kar os\u00e4kerheten kring regeringens stabilitet."], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.7, "rationale": "Authority gate: V can bind only itself. Its feasible self-binding declaration \u2014 confirming support/tolerance for the S-led minority government conditioned on a strong influence mechanism \u2014 is automatic and appears in both branches. The external component, securing a strong, visible, binding influence mechanism (formal cooperation agreement, budget mechanism, not being circumvented), requires S's acceptance and is not authoritatively established; f17d849a establishes binding policy agreements with V but not the structural influence mechanism. The desired effect's other components (S-led government as only credible alternative, Tid\u00f6 blocked, policy concessions delivered) are already established by active effects 3f692427, 8d4ca0fc, 9d31fe88 and f17d849a, and are not re-established by this action. Prerequisite gate: no deterministic rule applies. Plausibility: V's 29 mandates are pivotal and the policy agreements are already in place, making S likely to accommodate V's influence demand; however, tension with C's conditioned tolerance (enterprise, decentralization, fiscal framework) and S's preference for a narrower package leaves genuine residual uncertainty. Probability 0.70.", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": ["V bekr\u00e4ftar sitt st\u